ineural hearing loss with pure-tone thresholds of 30 dB in the left ear and 35 dB in the right ear within the 500-2,000 Hz range, speech audiometry thresholds of 50 dB in the left ear and 60 dB in the right ear, and speech discrimination abilities of 32% at 80 dB in the left ear and 20% at 85 dB in the right ear; brainstem auditory evoked potential responses were normal; she recognized six out of eight nonverbal animal sounds and correctly matched four out of six songs to their written titles; neuropsychological testing showed below-normal performance on the Korean version of the Boston Naming Test, ideomotor praxis, Rey figure-copying test, calculation, finger naming, and the semantic subtest of the controlled oral association word recall test; in a Navon figure task, she recognized only small letters; she had difficulty naming famous people but could describe the occupations of some she could not name; routine laboratory tests showed no evidence of comorbid disease."]}
